  "description": "Determine if a word exists in a grid of characters by moving to adjacent cells.",
  "target": "ABCC",
  "pseudocode": "1. for r in rows, c in cols: \n2. if dfs(r, c, 0): return true \n3. dfs(r, c, index): \n4. if index == word.len: return true \n5. if out of bounds or board[r][c] != word[index] or visited: return false \n6. mark visited \n7. if dfs(r+1, c, index+1) or dfs(r-1, c, index+1) or dfs(r, c+1, index+1) or dfs(r, c-1, index+1): return true \n8. backtrack: unmark visited",
